Problem: 217. Contains Duplicate

Approach:
- Use a HashSet to keep track of elements already seen.
- If the current element already exists in the HashSet, return true.
- Otherwise, add it to the HashSet.
- If no duplicates are found after traversing the array, return false.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Reason: Single traversal of the array with average O(1) HashSet operations.

Space Complexity: O(n)
Reason: In the worst case, all elements are unique and stored in the HashSet.

code->

class Solution {
    public boolean containsDuplicate(int[] nums) {
        HashSet<Integer> set=new HashSet<>();
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            if(set.contains(nums[i])){
                return true;
            }
            else{
                set.add(nums[i]);
            }
        }
        return false;
    }
}
